      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes perfect sense, doesn't it? When the weight is all you've got left, letting go feels like the only honest choice. But \"stop\" doesn't have to mean the end—it can mean putting the pen down for a while, not snapping it in half. You're not broken beyond repair; you're just exhausted from carrying a version of yourself that was never meant to last forever. Give yourself permission to rest, not to quit.",
